T*
(Engineering systems typically involve multivariable response surfaces where functions) Tj
T*
(depend on several independent physical variables z = f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(* Partial Derivatives: The partial derivative dz/dx is evaluated by differentiating) Tj
T*
(with respect to x while treating y strictly as a constant. Higher-order mixed) Tj
T*
(partials satisfy Clairaut's / Schwarz's Theorem: d^2z / \(dx dy\) = d^2z / \(dy dx\) if) Tj
T*
(partial derivatives are continuous.) Tj
T*
(* Homogeneous Functions: A function f\(x, y\) is homogeneous of degree n if f\(t*x, t*y\)) Tj
T*
(= t^n * f\(x, y\) for all scalars t > 0.) Tj
T*
(* Euler's Theorem for Homogeneous Functions:) Tj
T*
(If u = f\(x, y\) is a homogeneous function of x and y of degree n having continuous) Tj
T*
(partial derivatives, then:) Tj
T*
(x * \(du/dx\) + y * \(du/dy\) = n * u.) Tj
T*
(* Second Order Extension of Euler's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(x^2 * \(d^2u / dx^2\) + 2*x*y * \(d^2u / \(dx dy\)\) + y^2 * \(d^2u / dy^2\) = n * \(n - 1\) * u.) Tj
T*
