T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: If u = arcsin\([ x + y ] / [ sqrt\(x\) + sqrt\(y\) ]\), prove that x*\(du/dx\) +) Tj
T*
(y*\(du/dy\) = \(1/2\) * tan\(u\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Let z = sin\(u\) = [ x + y ] / [ sqrt\(x\) + sqrt\(y\) ].) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Determine homogeneity and degree of z:) Tj
T*
(Numerator N\(x, y\) = x + y is homogeneous of degree 1.) Tj
T*
(Denominator D\(x, y\) = sqrt\(x\) + sqrt\(y\) is homogeneous of degree 1/2.) Tj
T*
(z\(tx, ty\) = [ tx + ty ] / [ sqrt\(tx\) + sqrt\(ty\) ] = [ t*\(x + y\) ] / [ t^{1/2}*\(sqrt\(x\) +) Tj
T*
(sqrt\(y\)\) ]) Tj
T*
(= t^{1 - 1/2} * z\(x, y\) = t^{1/2} * z\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(Thus, z is a homogeneous function of x and y of degree n = 1/2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Apply Euler's Theorem to z:) Tj
T*
(x * \(dz/dx\) + y * \(dz/dy\) = n * z = \(1/2\) * z.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Express derivatives in terms of u:) Tj
T*
(Since z = sin\(u\), dz/dx = cos\(u\) * \(du/dx\) and dz/dy = cos\(u\) * \(du/dy\).) Tj
T*
(Substitute: x * [ cos\(u\) * \(du/dx\) ] + y * [ cos\(u\) * \(du/dy\) ] = \(1/2\) * sin\(u\).) Tj
T*
(Factor cos\(u\): cos\(u\) * [ x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) ] = \(1/2\) * sin\(u\).) Tj
T*
(Divide by cos\(u\): x*\(du/dx\) + y*\(du/dy\) = \(1/2\) * [ sin\(u\) / cos\(u\) ] = \(1/2\) * tan\(u\).) Tj
T*
(\(Hence Proved\).) Tj
T*
