T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: For the Cartesian to polar transformation x = r*cos\(theta\), y = r*sin\(theta\),) Tj
T*
(calculate J = d\(x, y\)/d\(r, theta\) and J' = d\(r, theta\)/d\(x, y\), and verify J * J' = 1.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute partial derivatives for J:) Tj
T*
(dx/dr = cos\(theta\), dx/d\(theta\) = -r*sin\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(dy/dr = sin\(theta\), dy/d\(theta\) = r*cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Evaluate determinant J:) Tj
T*
(J = det\([ cos\(theta\) -r*sin\(theta\) ; sin\(theta\) r*cos\(theta\) ]\)) Tj
T*
(J = cos\(theta\) * [ r*cos\(theta\) ] - [ -r*sin\(theta\) ] * sin\(theta\) = r*cos^2\(theta\) +) Tj
T*
(r*sin^2\(theta\) = r.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Compute inverse relations:) Tj
T*
(r = sqrt\(x^2 + y^2\), theta = arctan\(y / x\).) Tj
T*
(dr/dx = x / sqrt\(x^2 + y^2\) = x / r = cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(dr/dy = y / sqrt\(x^2 + y^2\) = y / r = sin\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(d\(theta\)/dx = [ 1 / \(1 + \(y/x\)^2\) ] * \(-y / x^2\) = -y / \(x^2 + y^2\) = -sin\(theta\) / r.) Tj
T*
(d\(theta\)/dy = [ 1 / \(1 + \(y/x\)^2\) ] * \(1 / x\) = x / \(x^2 + y^2\) = cos\(theta\) / r.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 4: Evaluate determinant J':) Tj
T*
(J' = det\([ cos\(theta\) sin\(theta\) ; -sin\(theta\)/r cos\(theta\)/r ]\)) Tj
T*
(J' = [ cos\(theta\) * cos\(theta\)/r ] - [ sin\(theta\) * \(-sin\(theta\)/r\) ] = \(cos^2 + sin^2\)) Tj
T*
(/ r = 1 / r.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 5: Verification of Reciprocal Property:) Tj
T*
(J * J' = r * \(1 / r\) = 1. \(Verified\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
