([SOLVED PROBLEM 3: Complete Classification of Multivariable Extrema]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem: Find and classify all critical points of the function f\(x, y\) = x^3 + y^3 - 3*x) Tj
T*
(- 12*y + 20.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Compute first partial derivatives and set to zero:) Tj
T*
(fx = 3*x^2 - 3 = 0 => 3*\(x^2 - 1\) = 0 => x = +1 or x = -1.) Tj
T*
(fy = 3*y^2 - 12 = 0 => 3*\(y^2 - 4\) = 0 => y = +2 or y = -2.) Tj
T*
(There are 4 distinct critical points: P1\(1, 2\), P2\(1, -2\), P3\(-1, 2\), P4\(-1, -2\).) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Compute second partial derivatives:) Tj
T*
(r = fxx = 6*x, s = fxy = 0, t = fyy = 6*y.) Tj
T*
(Discriminant: Delta = r*t - s^2 = \(6*x\)*\(6*y\) - 0 = 36*x*y.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Classify each point:) Tj
T*
(1. Point P1\(1, 2\): Delta = 36*\(1\)*\(2\) = +72 > 0. r = 6*\(1\) = +6 > 0. Conclusion: LOCAL) Tj
T*
(MINIMUM.) Tj
T*
(Minimum Value: f\(1, 2\) = 1 + 8 - 3 - 24 + 20 = 2.) Tj
T*
(2. Point P2\(1, -2\): Delta = 36*\(1\)*\(-2\) = -72 < 0. Conclusion: SADDLE POINT.) Tj
T*
(3. Point P3\(-1, 2\): Delta = 36*\(-1\)*\(2\) = -72 < 0. Conclusion: SADDLE POINT.) Tj
T*
(4. Point P4\(-1, -2\): Delta = 36*\(-1\)*\(-2\) = +72 > 0. r = 6*\(-1\) = -6 < 0. Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(LOCAL MAXIMUM.) Tj
T*
(Maximum Value: f\(-1, -2\) = -1 - 8 + 3 + 24 + 20 = 38.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
